From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc64: leave the lock bit out of the MMU's translations
 property

The "translations" property listed the firmware's own locked mappings
(its text and its heap, above the kernel base) with the TTE lock bit
set. When Solaris 2.5.1 takes the firmware's translations over it
panics on a locked translation that isn't global ("map_prom: locked
translation is not global"), and 2.6 and later panic on a global one,
so OBP lists neither; Solaris 2.6 to 10 clear the lock bit themselves.

List the translations without the lock bit. The mappings themselves,
and the firmware's own TLB entries, stay as they were.
---
 arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c b/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c
index 5abc78b..9046b8b 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c
+++ b/arch/sparc64/ofmem_sparc64.c
@@ -99,7 +99,11 @@ void ofmem_arch_create_translation_entry(ucell *transentry, translation_t *t)
 
 	transentry[0] = t->virt;
 	transentry[1] = t->size;
-	transentry[2] = t->phys | t->mode | SPITFIRE_TTE_VALID;
+	/* Without the lock bit, as OBP lists its own locked mappings: Solaris
+	   2.5.1 panics on a locked translation that isn't global, and 2.6 and
+	   later on a global one; both clear the lock bit when they take the
+	   translations over */
+	transentry[2] = t->phys | (t->mode & ~SPITFIRE_TTE_LOCKED) | SPITFIRE_TTE_VALID;
 }
 
 /* Return the size of a memory available entry given the phandle in cells */
